1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,657
MY DEAR LIZZY

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:03,854
When I wrote that letter

3
00:00:04,418 --> 00:00:06,821
Tell me once for all,
are you engaged to him?

4
00:00:07,498 --> 00:00:10,471
You may ask questions which
I shall not choose to answer.

5
00:00:11,551 --> 00:00:14,240
How you must have hated
me after that evening?

6
00:00:15,351 --> 00:00:17,316
I will make no promise of the kind.

7
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:20,191
I am afraid you will be angry.

8
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,429
But I have an aunt, too, who
must not be longer neglected.

9
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,396
It taught me to hope

10
00:00:26,795 --> 00:00:28,683
Indeed, you are mistaken, Madam.

11
00:00:28,936 --> 00:00:31,762
Bennet, delighted to
speak to Lady Catherine.

12
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:35,449
My dear Lizzy, where can
you have been walking to?

13
00:00:36,093 --> 00:00:38,899
That is to say, you had
given your permission.

14
00:00:39,763 --> 00:00:43,225
Never had his wit been directed in
a manner so little agreeable to her.

15
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:45,260
I know it to be impossible.

16
00:00:45,931 --> 00:00:47,806
I am sorry, exceedingly sorry
